{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Day 19 — Pandas transformation: groupby, agg, pivot_table, melt\n","Objectives:\n","- Summarize with groupby and custom aggregations.\n","- Reshape data with pivot_table and melt.\n","- Combine multiple metrics and format outputs."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["import pandas as pd, numpy as np, seaborn as sns\n","df = sns.load_dataset('tips')\n","# Groupby with multiple aggregations\n","agg = df.groupby(['day','time']).agg(\n","    total_bill_mean=('total_bill','mean'),\n","    tip_mean=('tip','mean'),\n","    count=('total_bill','size'),\n",")\n","agg.reset_index().head()\n","\n","# Pivot table\n","pt = pd.pivot_table(df, values='tip', index='day', columns='time', aggfunc='mean')\n","pt\n","\n","# Melt back to long\n","long = pt.reset_index().melt(id_vars='day', var_name='time', value_name='avg_tip')\n","long.head()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Exercises\n","1) Compute total revenue and average tip by (day, smoker).\n","2) Create a pivot table of average tip by (day x time) and fill missing with 0.\n","3) Melt a wide DataFrame to long and then groupby to validate totals match original."]}]}
